hclient will not refresh it on its own", "netstat -rn still routes default via 198.51.100.1 on vtnet0 (not a routing-table fault), while the LAN 10.20.0.0/16 via vtnet1 is intact, matching 'local services still work'"], "action": "change_config", "recommendation": "Renew the WAN session on gw.lan - reconfigure vtnet0 / renew its DHCP lease (wan_reload) so it picks up a fresh address from the now-OPERATIONAL cable modem; the watchdog's own 02:30 decision was to reload but, being in observe mode, it only logged would_reload. Afterwards ask the ISP why the modem could not fetch its config file (TFTP NOT FOUND), and consider taking the watchdog out of observe mode so a post-registration WAN reload happens automatically.", "detail": "Stale WAN DHCP session after ISP-side modem re-provision; never renewed", "contributing": {"host": "external", "component": "provider_network"}}}
